tps://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-04-15T10:00:11Z","updated_at":"2026-05-19T16:26:03Z","closed_at":"2026-05-19T16:22:56Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible  in: 4.6.2-stable\n- Not reproducible in: 4.5.2-stable\n\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.2.stable - macOS Sequoia (15.6.1) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Metal (Mobile) - integrated Apple M4 Pro (Apple9) - Apple M4 Pro (12 threads) - 48.00 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\n\niOS plugins that register a service via `GDTApplicationDelegate.addService:` and implement `application:openURL:options:` do not receive URL callbacks when the app is opened via a custom URL scheme.\n\nGodot 4.6 uses SwiftUI's `@main struct App` with `@UIApplicationDelegateAdaptor`. In scene-based apps, iOS delivers URLs via `scene(_:openURLContexts:)` on the scene delegate, not via `application(_:open:options:)` on the app delegate. Since Godot does not handle this, URLs are silently dropped.\n\n### Possible fix (not verified)\n\nOne approach would be to add `.onOpenURL` modifier to `app.swift` to forward URLs to the app delegate:\n\n```swift\nvar body: some Scene {\n    WindowGroup {\n        GodotSwiftUIViewController()\n            .ignoresSafeArea()\n            .onOpenURL { url in\n                _ = appDelegate.application(UIApplication.shared, open: url, options: [:])\n            }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open the MRP project (`godot_app/`) in Godot 4.6.2.\n2. Enable the \"MRP URL Test\" editor plugin (Project → Project Settings → Plugins).\n3. In the iOS export preset, enable the \"MRPURLTest\" plugin under the Plugins section.\n4. Export to iOS and deploy to a physical device via Xcode.\n5. Launch the app and confirm `MRP: Service registered to GDTApplicationDelegate` appears in the Xcode console.\n6. Open Safari on the device and navigate to `godotmrptest://hello`.\n7. The app opens (URL scheme is registered correctly).\n\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[MRP.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/26744934/MRP.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":